.TH LUS-COMPILE 1 "" "Lus" "Lus Manual"
.SH NAME
lus-compile \- compile a script to a binary chunk
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBlus compile\fR [options] script
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Compiles a script to a binary chunk, which \fBlus\fR runs as it runs a script and \fBload\fR reads in binary mode.
Loading a binary chunk skips parsing.
A binary chunk can be distributed without its source.
The default output is the script name with the extension \fB.lusc\fR.
Binary chunks describes the format.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-o FILE\fR
Write the chunk to \fBFILE\fR.
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-strip\fR
Omit debug information, which makes the chunk smaller and removes line numbers from its error messages.
.TP
\fB\-F name[=value]\fR, \fB\-\-flag name[=value]\fR
Define a build flag, whose value is fixed in the chunk.
.TP
\fB\-P perm\fR, \fB\-\-pledge perm\fR
Grant a permission to the initializers of \fB<meta>\fR variables, which run during the compilation.
The chunk itself runs with the permissions of the command that runs it.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
0
The chunk was written.
.TP
1
The script does not compile or the chunk cannot be written.
.TP
2
An option is malformed.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lus (1)
.PP
The CLI page of the Lus manual, https://lus.dev/manual/cli#lus-compile, has the same text with links to the rest of the manual.
